🐛 Describe the bug
Not sure if this is intended behavior or not. I guess I found silent errors to be annoying. It would be nice to have a debug mode where these kind of things are enforced.
I have a custom op, where the meta function and the actual custom op would return different shapes. There is a view followed by the custom op, so I expect an error caused by viewing with a wrong shape. However, it ran successfully.
repro:
import torch

torch.library.define(
    "henrylhtsang::square_fn",
    "(Tensor q) -> Tensor",
)


@torch.library.impl("henrylhtsang::square_fn", "Meta")
def square_fn_meta(
    query: torch.Tensor,
):
    return torch.empty_like(query)


@torch.library.impl("henrylhtsang::square_fn", "CUDA")
def square_fn(
    query: torch.Tensor,
) -> torch.Tensor:
    query_shape = query.shape[:-1] + (2048,)
    return torch.empty(query_shape, dtype=query.dtype, device=query.device)


def main() -> None:
    class Model(torch.nn.Module):
        def forward(self, x):
            return torch.ops.henrylhtsang.square_fn(x).view(x.shape)

    tensor = torch.randn(1024, 1024, device="cuda", dtype=torch.float16)
    model = Model().cuda()

    ep = torch.export.export(model, (tensor,))
    path = torch._inductor.aoti_compile_and_package(
        ep,
        (tensor,),
    )
    aot_model = torch._inductor.aoti_load_package(path)
    aot_model(tensor)

    print("done")


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()

Expected outcome:
failed with an error
Actual outcome:
finished without an error.
